  "<strong>Tactless Autist</strong> wrote <em>proton-calendar-sync</em> and the <em>proton-calendar-client</em> library it builds on. <a href=\"#\" class=\"external-link\" data-href=\"https://github.com/TactlessAutist\">github.com/TactlessAutist</a>": [
    "index.html (html)"
  ],
  "<strong>Tobi</strong> forked it as <em>Neutron Calendar Bridge</em> and added what makes it a daily driver: meetings like in Proton Calendar (invitations, answers, updates and cancellations emailed from your calendar app, end-to-end to Proton users, in Proton's 34 languages), repeating events and reminders in both directions, Thunderbird and other CalDAV apps, several accounts, Proton Meet and Zoom links, offline edits, one-click setup, the sign-in under the bridge's own name, automatic updates, six languages — and privacy throughout: an encrypted local copy, a quiet log, nothing reported anywhere. <a href=\"#\" class=\"external-link\" data-href=\"https://github.com/to-bi-s/neutron-calendar-bridge\">github.com/to-bi-s/neutron-calendar-bridge</a>": [
